WEBVTT

00:00:05.364 --> 00:00:39.809
Oxford bookworms stage one published by FLTRP copyright Oxford University Press 2009 Mary Queen of Scots by Tim Vickery read by Claire Willy chapter one fathering gay My name is Best Curl, but this is not my story.

00:00:39.869 --> 00:00:46.442
It is the story of my Lady Mary, Queen of Scots.

00:00:46.502 --> 00:00:51.994
She wrote the story, and then she gave it to me.

00:00:52.054 --> 00:00:56.826
I am going to give it to her son.

00:00:56.886 --> 00:01:01.929
She began the story a week ago.

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:17.048
It was January 1587 and we sat here in our cold room in Fotheringay Castle in the north of England.

00:01:17.108 --> 00:01:21.460
We couldn't see much from the window.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:32.524
One or two houses, a river, some trees, some horses and a road.

00:01:32.584 --> 00:01:41.639
The road goes to London, the home of Queen Elizabeth of England.

00:01:41.698 --> 00:01:51.414
Mary sat with her little dog in her hands and watched it all day long.

00:01:51.474 --> 00:01:55.156
No one came along the road.

00:01:55.216 --> 00:01:57.928
Nothing happened.

00:01:57.988 --> 00:02:02.345
I watched Mary unhappily.

00:02:02.405 --> 00:02:08.872
Please your Majesty, come away from that window," I said.

00:02:08.932 --> 00:02:11.002
It doesn't help.

00:02:11.062 --> 00:02:14.074
No one is going to come.

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:17.634
Queen Elizabeth can't do it.

00:02:17.694 --> 00:02:21.796
Queens don't kill queens.

00:02:21.856 --> 00:02:24.477
Don't they, Bass?

00:02:24.536 --> 00:02:26.197
Mary said.

00:02:26.257 --> 00:02:30.178
Then why are we here in this prison?

00:02:30.238 --> 00:02:33.670
Why am I not free?

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.903
Why, your Majesty?

00:02:36.963 --> 00:02:41.276
Because Queen Elizabeth is afraid of you."

00:02:41.336 --> 00:02:45.368
That's right, Mary said.

00:02:45.427 --> 00:02:50.170
She's afraid of me, and she hates me too.

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:56.618
She hates me because I am beautiful, and she is not.

00:02:56.678 --> 00:03:02.715
because I had three husbands, and she never married.

00:03:02.774 --> 00:03:18.632
And because many people, good Catholic people in England, France, Scotland, Spain, say that I marry and the true queen of England, not Elizabeth.

00:03:18.692 --> 00:03:33.300
And Elizabeth has no children, so when she is dead, my son, James, She came away from the window and stood in front of me.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.694
James, she said quietly.

00:03:37.754 --> 00:03:40.166
My son.

00:03:40.226 --> 00:03:42.918
Does he think about me?

00:03:42.978 --> 00:03:44.870
Sometimes.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:51.034
He was only ten months old when I last saw him.

00:03:51.094 --> 00:03:55.700
It is nearly twenty years.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:04:02.304
Of course he thinks about you, your Majesty," I said.

00:04:02.364 --> 00:04:04.756
You write to him often.

00:04:04.816 --> 00:04:08.358
How can he forget his mother?

00:04:08.418 --> 00:04:12.740
Then why doesn't he write to me?

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:15.221
Mary asked.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:20.603
Does he want me to stay here in an English prison?

00:04:20.663 --> 00:04:24.786
No, of course not your Majesty.

00:04:24.846 --> 00:04:28.330
He has a lot of work, Your Majesty.

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:38.487
He is the King of Scotland, and he is not the King of Scotland best, she said.

00:04:38.547 --> 00:04:41.319
Not before I am dead.

00:04:41.379 --> 00:04:43.370
Remember that.

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.652
No, Your Majesty.

00:04:45.712 --> 00:04:47.314
Of course not.

00:04:47.374 --> 00:04:53.098
But perhaps people tell him things that are untrue.

00:04:53.158 --> 00:04:56.343
You know what people say.

00:04:56.403 --> 00:04:58.186
Perhaps.

00:04:58.246 --> 00:05:03.364
Perhaps he thinks you killed his father.

00:05:03.424 --> 00:05:06.758
Mary's face went white.

00:05:06.818 --> 00:05:09.058
She was very angry.

00:05:09.118 --> 00:05:12.539
And for a minute, I was afraid.

00:05:12.599 --> 00:05:18.350
She said, You know that's a lie, Bess.

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:20.380
It is a lie.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:24.251
I did not kill James' father.

00:05:24.311 --> 00:05:27.442
I knew nothing about it.

00:05:27.502 --> 00:05:30.892
I know that, Your Majesty.

00:05:30.952 --> 00:05:34.988
But perhaps James doesn't know it.

00:05:35.048 --> 00:05:40.094
He hears so many lies all the time.

00:05:40.154 --> 00:05:44.056
He needs to know the true story.

00:05:44.116 --> 00:05:49.658
Why don't you write and tell him?

00:05:49.718 --> 00:05:53.800
Mary sat down slowly.

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:57.872
She looked old and tired.

00:05:57.932 --> 00:06:01.004
All right, Bess.

00:06:01.064 --> 00:06:05.650
She said, give me a pen, please.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:12.061
I'm going to write to James and tell him the true story.

00:06:12.121 --> 00:06:16.686
You can give it to him when I'm dead.

00:06:16.746 --> 00:06:19.788
Dead, your Majesty.

00:06:19.848 --> 00:06:22.071
Don't say that.

00:06:22.131 --> 00:06:25.024
You aren't going to die.

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:29.460
Her old, tired eyes looked at me.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:32.894
Yes, I am, Bess.

00:06:32.954 --> 00:06:36.066
You know what is going to happen.

00:06:36.126 --> 00:06:47.852
One day soon, a man is going to bring a letter from Queen Elizabeth, and then her men are going to kill me.

00:06:47.912 --> 00:06:55.786
But before I die, I would like to write to my son, James.

00:06:55.846 --> 00:07:02.061
I want to tell him The story of my life.

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:06.836
So give me a pen please.

00:07:06.896 --> 00:07:10.500
I gave her a pen.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:23.792
This is what she wrote.

00:07:23.852 --> 00:07:49.744
Chapter 2 France Dear James, very soon I am going to die and meet my God.

00:07:49.804 --> 00:07:58.268
Before I die, I want to write the true story of my life for you.

00:07:58.328 --> 00:08:03.710
Everything that I write here is true.

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:09.324
I cannot lie to you or to God.

00:08:09.384 --> 00:08:12.586
Please believe that, James.

00:08:12.646 --> 00:08:15.508
It's important to me.

00:08:15.568 --> 00:08:21.093
My father died when I was one week old.

00:08:21.152 --> 00:08:27.317
So I was the queen of Scots when I was a baby.

00:08:27.377 --> 00:08:33.001
At first, I lived with my mother in Scotland.

00:08:33.062 --> 00:08:38.644
And then, when I was five, I went to France.

00:08:38.704 --> 00:08:47.240
My mother was French, but she stayed in Scotland and died there.

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:53.534
I went to France to marry the King of France's son.

00:08:53.594 --> 00:08:57.116
His name was Francis.

00:08:57.176 --> 00:09:01.257
and he was one year younger than me.

00:09:01.316 --> 00:09:10.672
In 1559, his father died, so Francis was king.

00:09:10.732 --> 00:09:17.716
Then I was queen of France and queen of Scotland too.

00:09:17.776 --> 00:09:21.839
I was very happy in France.

00:09:21.898 --> 00:09:27.336
Francis my husband was like a little brother to me.

00:09:27.397 --> 00:09:40.772
I think he loved me but he was very young and he was often ill and then in 1560 he died.

00:09:40.832 --> 00:09:44.424
He was 16 years old.

00:09:44.484 --> 00:09:52.316
When he died I was very unhappy and my life was very different.

00:09:52.376 --> 00:10:00.026
There was a new king and queen, and I wasn't important in France anymore.

00:10:00.086 --> 00:10:04.048
But I was still queen of Scots.

00:10:04.108 --> 00:10:09.401
So, I came back to Scotland.

00:10:09.461 --> 00:10:16.656
When I arrived in Scotland, I was a young girl of 18.

00:10:16.716 --> 00:10:22.967
My mother was dead, and there was no one there to meet me.

00:10:23.027 --> 00:10:30.969
I walked off the ship and I slept in a little house near the sea.

00:10:31.029 --> 00:10:37.142
Next day the Scots lords came from Edinburgh.

00:10:37.202 --> 00:10:43.696
They were pleased to see me and for a week everyone was happy.

00:10:43.756 --> 00:10:48.720
People smiled at me and sang in the streets.

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:52.150
I think everyone liked me.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:58.107
Then, that Sunday, I went to church.

00:10:58.167 --> 00:11:07.981
James, my son, you are a Protestant, and I am a Catholic.

00:11:08.041 --> 00:11:17.820
You are a good man and you love God, but your church and my church are enemies.

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:24.365
I was born a Catholic and I am going to die a Catholic.

00:11:24.425 --> 00:11:27.188
I love God too.

00:11:27.248 --> 00:11:30.040
I hope you understand that.

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:33.122
I'm not going to change now.

00:11:33.182 --> 00:11:42.796
That Sunday people shouted angrily in the streets Your Majesty, said the Scots lords.

00:11:42.856 --> 00:11:45.527
Scotland is a Protestant country.

00:11:45.587 --> 00:11:48.638
You can't go to a Catholic church here.

00:11:48.698 --> 00:11:52.940
The Scottish people don't like Catholics.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:57.761
I'm sorry, my lords, I said.

00:11:57.821 --> 00:12:00.152
But I am your queen.

00:12:00.212 --> 00:12:03.483
No one tells me what to do.

00:12:03.543 --> 00:12:09.294
I don't hate Protestants, and I'm not going to kill them.

00:12:09.353 --> 00:12:15.754
The people can go to their Protestant churches and pray to God there.

00:12:15.814 --> 00:12:22.348
But I'm going to pray with Catholics in my church.

00:12:22.408 --> 00:12:26.350
People were angry because of that.

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:31.642
A man called John Knox came to see me.

00:12:31.702 --> 00:12:35.894
He was a famous Protestant churchman.

00:12:35.954 --> 00:12:38.490
But I didn't like him.

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:43.972
He was a big, angry man with black clothes.

00:12:44.032 --> 00:12:52.402
He hated the Catholic Church and wanted all Catholics to leave Scotland.

00:12:52.462 --> 00:12:59.527
To him, the Protestant Church was the only true Church of God.

00:12:59.587 --> 00:13:06.717
He said, Your Majesty, you're a young woman like my daughter.

00:13:06.777 --> 00:13:12.890
Women can't understand difficult things like God or the church.

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:16.491
Find a good Protestant husband, girl.

00:13:16.551 --> 00:13:18.782
Let him rule this country for you.

00:13:18.802 --> 00:13:25.061
I was very angry with this man, Knox.

00:13:25.121 --> 00:13:29.778
I was a queen, but I was only eighteen.

00:13:29.838 --> 00:13:32.379
He didn't talk quietly.

00:13:32.439 --> 00:13:34.589
He shouted at me.

00:13:34.649 --> 00:13:38.170
I cried because of his angry words.

00:13:38.230 --> 00:13:40.931
I could not understand him.

00:13:40.991 --> 00:13:46.042
He talked so much, and he knew so many books.

00:13:46.102 --> 00:13:50.774
But I did not go to his church.

00:13:50.834 --> 00:13:54.954
He was right about one thing.

00:13:55.014 --> 00:14:10.687
Perhaps I could rule Scotland without a man, but I could not have a child without one, and every queen needs a son or daughter to come after her.

00:14:10.747 --> 00:14:24.105
So I began to look for a husband.

00:14:24.165 --> 00:14:38.881
chapter 3, Darnley and Riccio.

00:14:38.941 --> 00:14:46.794
At first I wanted to marry the son of the king of Spain, Don Carlos.

00:14:46.854 --> 00:14:55.138
But he was a Catholic, of course, and my Scots lords did not like that.

00:14:55.198 --> 00:14:58.961
It was difficult for me, James.

00:14:59.021 --> 00:15:01.954
I wanted to please myself.

00:15:02.014 --> 00:15:10.200
I wanted to please my friends and family in France and to please my people too.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:15.312
And then there was the Queen of England.

00:15:15.372 --> 00:15:21.464
At first I wanted very much to be friends with Elizabeth.

00:15:21.524 --> 00:15:30.808
We wrote many letters and talked about a meeting, a meeting between two sister queens.

00:15:30.868 --> 00:15:40.256
Elizabeth wrote to me at this time, our two countries need to be friends.

00:15:40.315 --> 00:15:43.298
You need a husband.

00:15:43.358 --> 00:15:46.129
I need a friend.

00:15:46.189 --> 00:15:53.330
Why not marry my friend Robert Dudley, the Earl of Leicester?

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:57.131
He is a tall, strong man.

00:15:57.191 --> 00:16:02.722
I think he could be a good husband for you.

00:16:02.782 --> 00:16:07.784
I was very angry about this letter.

00:16:07.844 --> 00:16:14.128
There were a lot of stories about Elizabeth and Robert Dudley.

00:16:14.188 --> 00:16:17.058
They were good friends.

00:16:17.118 --> 00:16:22.780
He often danced and sang and talked with her.

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:29.731
Sometimes, people said, he stayed in her room all night.

00:16:29.791 --> 00:16:33.202
Dudley had a wife.

00:16:33.262 --> 00:16:38.179
But one day, she died very suddenly.

00:16:38.239 --> 00:16:41.116
It was an accident.

00:16:41.176 --> 00:16:45.546
She fell down the stairs, they say.

00:16:45.606 --> 00:16:54.498
But then perhaps she was unhappy because of her husband and Elizabeth.

00:16:54.558 --> 00:17:01.280
And she writes to me about a man like this, I thought.

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:09.282
She wants him to marry me because he is her friend, her lover perhaps.

00:17:09.342 --> 00:17:15.113
She wants her lover to be King of Scotland.

00:17:15.174 --> 00:17:20.105
I found a better man than Dudley, James.

00:17:20.165 --> 00:17:25.617
I found Henry Dunley, your father.

00:17:25.676 --> 00:17:30.288
He was 19 years old, and I was 23.

00:17:30.348 --> 00:17:39.352
He was a tall man with a beautiful face and big green eyes.

00:17:39.412 --> 00:17:45.928
He talked and sang well, and I liked dancing with him.

00:17:45.988 --> 00:17:54.114
He often wore expensive black clothes, and he laughed a lot when he was with me.

00:17:54.174 --> 00:18:01.600
He was very young and friendly, and I felt happy when I was with him.

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:09.261
I liked him very much, and I thought he loved me too.

00:18:09.321 --> 00:18:13.049
He was an important man too.

00:18:13.109 --> 00:18:15.080
We were cousins.

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:25.600
His grandfather was King of Scots and his great grandfather was Henry VII of England.

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:31.604
In July 1565, I married him.

00:18:31.664 --> 00:18:46.272
Elizabeth was very angry and so were a lot of the Scots lords My half-brother, the Earl of Moray, tried to stop the marriage.

00:18:46.332 --> 00:18:52.414
I had to fight him, and he ran south to England.

00:18:52.474 --> 00:18:55.496
But I was happy.

00:18:55.556 --> 00:19:00.398
Your father and I laughed every day.

00:19:00.458 --> 00:19:05.950
He was now Henry, King of Scots.

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:13.116
After one or two weeks, The laughter stopped.

00:19:13.176 --> 00:19:16.797
A king has a lot of work, James.

00:19:16.857 --> 00:19:18.708
You know that.

00:19:18.768 --> 00:19:28.430
He has to read hundreds of letters, talk to people, and think about a lot of important things.

00:19:28.490 --> 00:19:32.682
I did those things every day.

00:19:32.742 --> 00:19:38.890
But now I thought I had a man to help me.

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:46.180
My Lord Henry, I said, would you like to read all the letters with me?

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:52.234
You can sit next to me, and you can work with me every day."

00:19:52.294 --> 00:19:56.077
Your father looked unhappy.

00:19:56.137 --> 00:20:02.070
I'm not interested in work like that, he said.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:04.994
I don't understand it.

00:20:05.054 --> 00:20:08.718
Of course not, I said.

00:20:08.778 --> 00:20:11.388
You're a young man, my love.

00:20:11.448 --> 00:20:14.558
But I can teach you.

00:20:14.618 --> 00:20:21.960
For one or two days, he sat down with me, and I tried to teach him.

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:24.961
But it was true.

00:20:25.021 --> 00:20:32.574
He was not interested in the work, and he did not try to understand it.

00:20:32.634 --> 00:20:37.016
You do it, Mary," he said.

00:20:37.076 --> 00:20:39.746
I'm going out with my friends.

00:20:39.806 --> 00:20:45.087
We're going to ride and drink and swim.

00:20:45.148 --> 00:20:49.558
So I did all the work.

00:20:49.618 --> 00:20:55.380
At night, too, he often went out with his friends in the town.

00:20:55.440 --> 00:21:03.096
They drank a lot and laughed and sang, and there were often fights.

00:21:03.156 --> 00:21:11.114
But no one said anything, because he was the king, my husband.

00:21:11.174 --> 00:21:14.595
What could people say?

00:21:14.655 --> 00:21:20.556
They were unhappy, but they were afraid of him.

00:21:20.616 --> 00:21:27.516
Some of them went to England, to the Earl of Moray.

00:21:27.576 --> 00:21:34.286
At this time, I was often very tired, because I was pregnant.

00:21:34.346 --> 00:21:40.668
You, my son James, were alive inside me.

00:21:40.729 --> 00:21:48.292
But I did all the work of a queen, and I needed friends too.

00:21:48.352 --> 00:21:53.174
One of these friends was a young Italian.

00:21:53.234 --> 00:21:56.502
David Ricchio.

00:21:56.562 --> 00:22:07.236
Riccio was a little man, and he was not tall or beautiful or strong.

00:22:07.296 --> 00:22:12.119
But he was a very clever, interesting man.

00:22:12.179 --> 00:22:17.913
He wrote many of my letters for me and helped me.

00:22:17.972 --> 00:22:26.182
He sang well too, and I sometimes sang with him in the evenings.

00:22:26.242 --> 00:22:29.840
I liked him very much.

00:22:29.900 --> 00:22:35.103
And at first, your father liked him too.

00:22:35.163 --> 00:22:41.597
But then Moray's friends began to talk about me and Riccio.

00:22:41.658 --> 00:22:49.182
David Riccio is in the Queen's rooms every night, they said to your father.

00:22:49.242 --> 00:22:52.884
She laughs and sings and dances with him.

00:22:52.944 --> 00:22:55.394
My lord, it is not right.

00:22:55.454 --> 00:22:59.977
He is not a Scotsman, and he is not her husband.

00:23:00.037 --> 00:23:03.000
He is always with her.

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:07.584
Perhaps they said other things too.

00:23:07.644 --> 00:23:09.866
I don't know.

00:23:09.926 --> 00:23:14.470
A lot of Scots lords listen to them.

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:22.231
But I tell you, James, before God, I did nothing wrong.

00:23:22.292 --> 00:23:26.738
David Riccio was a good man.

00:23:26.798 --> 00:23:30.921
He worked hard and he helped me.

00:23:30.981 --> 00:23:33.822
So of course I liked him.

00:23:33.882 --> 00:23:37.156
Your father did not work.

00:23:37.216 --> 00:23:43.400
He went out to the town every night with his friends and drank.

00:23:43.460 --> 00:23:58.422
And then one night your father came home.

00:23:58.482 --> 00:24:20.608
Chapter 4 The Death of David Riccio It was a Saturday evening in March 1566.

00:24:20.668 --> 00:24:24.580
I was in Edinburgh with some friends.

00:24:24.640 --> 00:24:30.804
David Riccio was there, with six or seven other people.

00:24:30.864 --> 00:24:38.787
We were in a small room, but there was a good dinner on the table, and we were happy.

00:24:38.847 --> 00:24:46.640
It was dark outside, but inside it was warm and friendly.

00:24:46.700 --> 00:24:51.632
Suddenly a door opened behind me.

00:24:51.692 --> 00:24:57.646
In the door was Henry Darnley, my husband.

00:24:57.706 --> 00:25:01.416
I stood up and smiled.

00:25:01.476 --> 00:25:04.096
Good evening, my lord.

00:25:04.156 --> 00:25:07.388
I said, please come in.

00:25:07.448 --> 00:25:10.561
Would you like something to eat?

00:25:10.621 --> 00:25:12.782
No, thank you.

00:25:12.842 --> 00:25:20.588
He said, I'm not hungry, but I want to sit next to you, wife.

00:25:20.648 --> 00:25:25.242
Please tell that man to move.

00:25:25.302 --> 00:25:32.708
A man got out of the chair next to me, and Darnley sat beside me.

00:25:32.768 --> 00:25:36.800
Then he put his arms around me.

00:25:36.860 --> 00:25:39.430
I did not like it.

00:25:39.490 --> 00:25:45.124
His face was hot, and his eyes looked unhappy.

00:25:45.184 --> 00:25:51.596
But I smiled and said, I'm happy to see you, my lord.

00:25:51.656 --> 00:25:54.398
Are you, Mary?

00:25:54.458 --> 00:25:56.149
He laughed.

00:25:56.209 --> 00:25:58.361
Are you really?

00:25:58.421 --> 00:26:01.643
Yes, of course, my Lord.

00:26:01.703 --> 00:26:09.925
But then the second door opened, and his friend, Lord Ruthven, stood there.

00:26:09.985 --> 00:26:13.246
He had a knife in his hand.

00:26:13.306 --> 00:26:19.388
His face was red, and he looked very angry.

00:26:19.448 --> 00:26:23.488
But first no one moved.

00:26:23.548 --> 00:26:32.194
Then Ruthven said, Your Majesty, send David Riccio out of this room now.

00:26:32.254 --> 00:26:34.555
I want him."

00:26:34.615 --> 00:26:37.498
I looked at Riccio.

00:26:37.558 --> 00:26:39.999
He was afraid.

00:26:40.059 --> 00:26:41.820
Why?

00:26:41.880 --> 00:26:43.262
I said.

00:26:43.322 --> 00:26:45.852
Why do you want him?

00:26:45.912 --> 00:26:49.856
He is a bad, wicked man.

00:26:49.916 --> 00:26:54.104
Ruthven said, send him out.

00:26:54.164 --> 00:26:59.674
No, I said, you want to kill him.

00:26:59.734 --> 00:27:02.698
David Riccio is my friend.

00:27:02.758 --> 00:27:06.110
He stays here with me.

00:27:06.170 --> 00:27:09.492
He goes out, woman.

00:27:09.552 --> 00:27:15.868
Lord Ruthven said, King Henry, hold your wife, please.

00:27:15.928 --> 00:27:22.749
I stood up, but darnly held my arms, and I could not move.

00:27:22.809 --> 00:27:28.198
David Ricciot ran behind me and held my dress.

00:27:28.258 --> 00:27:35.402
My friends in the room stood up, too, and moved towards Ruthven angrily.

00:27:35.462 --> 00:27:39.476
But he had a knife in his hand.

00:27:39.536 --> 00:27:43.648
Get back, he said angrily.

00:27:43.708 --> 00:27:45.650
Don't touch me.

00:27:45.710 --> 00:27:57.087
Then five men with knives ran into the little room, and there was a fight One man held a knife in my face.

00:27:57.148 --> 00:28:02.248
And another man hit David Ricchio behind me.

00:28:02.308 --> 00:28:05.669
Then they pulled him out of the room.

00:28:05.729 --> 00:28:08.910
Help me, he screamed.

00:28:08.970 --> 00:28:11.500
Help me, my queen, please.

00:28:11.560 --> 00:28:13.190
They're going to kill me.

00:28:13.250 --> 00:28:15.961
Don't...

00:28:16.021 --> 00:28:22.324
I couldn't help him, because Darnley had me in his arms.

00:28:22.384 --> 00:28:26.506
But I could hear David Riccio's screams.

00:28:26.566 --> 00:28:29.567
I think he fell down the stairs.

00:28:29.627 --> 00:28:33.778
And he screamed for two or three minutes.

00:28:33.838 --> 00:28:37.579
Then it was quiet.

00:28:37.640 --> 00:28:40.530
What are you doing?

00:28:40.590 --> 00:28:43.341
I asked Darnley angrily.

00:28:43.401 --> 00:28:46.162
Riccio is a good man.

00:28:46.222 --> 00:28:48.842
Why are you doing this?

00:28:48.902 --> 00:28:51.676
Darnley laughed.

00:28:51.736 --> 00:28:59.644
You are my wife, Mary, not David Riccios," he said.

00:28:59.704 --> 00:29:03.206
So why are you with him every evening?

00:29:03.266 --> 00:29:05.108
You never talk to me.

00:29:05.128 --> 00:29:11.012
I don't talk to you because you are never here.

00:29:11.072 --> 00:29:15.524
I said, you are always drinking with your friends.

00:29:15.585 --> 00:29:17.135
You aren't a king.

00:29:17.155 --> 00:29:20.566
You're a stupid boy.

00:29:20.626 --> 00:29:23.246
He laughed again.

00:29:23.307 --> 00:29:26.720
It was not a nice laugh.

00:29:26.780 --> 00:29:33.054
Well, he said, perhaps I am a boy.

00:29:33.114 --> 00:29:37.729
But that is better than David Riccio now.

00:29:37.789 --> 00:29:41.582
Do you want to go and see him?

00:29:41.642 --> 00:29:47.177
I did see him, five minutes after that.

00:29:47.237 --> 00:29:50.142
He was very dead.

00:29:50.202 --> 00:29:54.387
and there was blood all over the floor.

00:29:54.447 --> 00:29:59.042
Paul David Riccio.

00:29:59.102 --> 00:30:05.487
He sings to God now, not me.

00:30:05.547 --> 00:30:10.991
I looked at Henry Darnley, my husband.

00:30:11.052 --> 00:30:15.145
He had a stupid smile on his face.

00:30:15.206 --> 00:30:19.262
But I think he was afraid of me.

00:30:19.322 --> 00:30:26.342
I looked at him a long time and the smile went away.

00:30:26.402 --> 00:30:36.211
Remember this night, husband, I said to him, remember it well.

00:30:36.271 --> 00:30:44.728
Think about it when you look into my eyes and before you go to sleep.

00:30:44.788 --> 00:30:53.646
David Ricciot was my friend, and you killed him in front of me.

00:30:53.706 --> 00:30:59.120
I'm never going to forget that, Henry Darnley.

00:30:59.180 --> 00:31:09.857
Never.

00:31:09.918 --> 00:31:21.104
chapter 5.

00:31:21.164 --> 00:31:25.006
My son is born.

00:31:25.067 --> 00:31:30.840
Next morning, Darnley came to see me.

00:31:30.900 --> 00:31:33.840
He was afraid.

00:31:33.901 --> 00:31:37.032
What's the matter husband?

00:31:37.092 --> 00:31:38.743
I said.

00:31:38.803 --> 00:31:42.250
Why are you crying?

00:31:42.310 --> 00:31:47.710
Mary, Mary, he said.

00:31:47.770 --> 00:31:51.001
I'm sorry, I was wrong.

00:31:51.062 --> 00:31:57.857
I helped those men to kill Riccio, and now the Earl of Moray is back here with them.

00:31:57.917 --> 00:31:59.738
He hates me.

00:31:59.798 --> 00:32:04.252
I'm afraid they're going to kill me and you too.

00:32:04.312 --> 00:32:10.036
Think of our child, Mary, here inside you.

00:32:10.096 --> 00:32:14.163
He took me in his arms again.

00:32:14.223 --> 00:32:17.597
I was very angry.

00:32:17.658 --> 00:32:23.750
I am sorry, James, that this man was your father.

00:32:23.810 --> 00:32:28.690
He was a stupid boy, not a man.

00:32:28.750 --> 00:32:40.173
He was tall and strong and beautiful, but he could never think like a man or a king.

00:32:40.234 --> 00:32:45.584
I said, You know these men, Henry?

00:32:45.644 --> 00:32:49.364
What do they want?

00:32:49.423 --> 00:32:54.104
They want our child, Mary.

00:32:54.164 --> 00:32:56.415
They don't want us.

00:32:56.475 --> 00:32:59.546
They're going to put you in prison.

00:32:59.606 --> 00:33:02.726
They don't want you to be queen.

00:33:02.786 --> 00:33:07.497
They want your child to be king or queen.

00:33:07.557 --> 00:33:13.798
I don't know what they want to do with me.

00:33:13.858 --> 00:33:23.842
Perhaps they want you to be king too, without me, I said quietly.

00:33:23.902 --> 00:33:30.814
Then you can do what they say, like a little boy.

00:33:30.874 --> 00:33:35.896
Perhaps, Mary, they said that yesterday.

00:33:35.956 --> 00:33:41.148
But now that Maury's here, I don't know, I'm afraid.

00:33:41.208 --> 00:33:43.537
Please help me.

00:33:43.597 --> 00:33:46.446
he began to cry again.

00:33:46.506 --> 00:33:49.076
What can we do?

00:33:49.136 --> 00:33:53.498
We can run away, I said.

00:33:53.558 --> 00:34:00.630
We can leave Edinburgh quickly and quietly before Ruthven and his men stop us.

00:34:00.690 --> 00:34:03.330
Be quiet for a minute.

00:34:03.390 --> 00:34:06.111
I want to think.

00:34:06.171 --> 00:34:11.032
I walked up and down for two or three minutes.

00:34:11.093 --> 00:34:18.344
Then I said, Henry, go back to these men.

00:34:18.404 --> 00:34:20.066
Tell them?

00:34:20.126 --> 00:34:21.458
No.

00:34:21.518 --> 00:34:23.400
Mary, please.

00:34:23.460 --> 00:34:24.982
I can't.

00:34:25.042 --> 00:34:27.576
I'm afraid of them.

00:34:27.635 --> 00:34:33.122
Listen to me, Henry, and try to be a man.

00:34:33.183 --> 00:35:16.062
go and tell them I'm ill because of the child say I'm not angry with them tell them anything lie to them then tonight bring some men and horses here behind the castle he went and did it all day I waited in my rooms and listened Then, at one o'clock in the morning, Darnley and I went quietly down the stairs behind the castle.

00:35:16.122 --> 00:35:21.964
Some of my friends were there, with horses for us.

00:35:22.024 --> 00:35:26.956
Quickly, we rode away into the night.

00:35:27.016 --> 00:35:30.752
That was a very bad night.

00:35:30.812 --> 00:35:34.518
It was dark and cold.

00:35:34.578 --> 00:35:40.242
I was ill, and Darnley was afraid.

00:35:40.303 --> 00:35:44.315
Come on, he said.

00:35:44.375 --> 00:35:46.797
Ride faster, woman.

00:35:46.857 --> 00:35:49.218
You're too slow.

00:35:49.278 --> 00:35:55.612
But I was pregnant, and it was cold and dark.

00:35:55.672 --> 00:35:59.925
We rode for five hours in the rain.

00:35:59.985 --> 00:36:02.976
I can't, Henry."

00:36:03.036 --> 00:36:04.577
I said.

00:36:04.637 --> 00:36:06.318
I'm ill.

00:36:06.378 --> 00:36:08.119
Think of the baby.

00:36:08.139 --> 00:36:11.891
I don't want it to die.

00:36:11.951 --> 00:36:14.202
Why not?

00:36:14.262 --> 00:36:15.613
He said.

00:36:15.673 --> 00:36:19.425
We can always make another one.

00:36:19.485 --> 00:36:23.898
I'm sorry, but it is true.

00:36:23.958 --> 00:36:28.568
Your father said things like that, James.

00:36:28.628 --> 00:36:36.733
Then he rode away in front of me, into the dark.

00:36:36.753 --> 00:36:43.698
I rode slowly behind, with my good woman, Bess Co.

00:36:43.759 --> 00:36:49.834
In the morning we arrived at Dunbar Castle.

00:36:49.894 --> 00:37:01.098
Darnley slept, and I wrote letters to my friends Next day, Lord Bothwell came to help me.

00:37:01.158 --> 00:37:03.259
I liked him.

00:37:03.319 --> 00:37:07.542
He was a good, strong man.

00:37:07.602 --> 00:37:13.496
Soon I had an army of 8,000 men.

00:37:13.556 --> 00:37:19.199
Bothwell and I rode back to Edinburgh with the army.

00:37:19.260 --> 00:37:25.313
Lord Ruthhen died, and some of his friends ran away.

00:37:25.373 --> 00:37:29.456
but the Earl of Moray stayed.

00:37:29.516 --> 00:37:37.502
All that summer I ruled the country and waited for the baby.

00:37:37.562 --> 00:37:42.205
My husband stayed outside my rooms.

00:37:42.265 --> 00:37:45.288
I did not want to see him.

00:37:45.348 --> 00:37:47.208
No one did.

00:37:47.268 --> 00:37:50.431
Perhaps he drank with his friends.

00:37:50.492 --> 00:37:52.876
I don't know.

00:37:52.937 --> 00:38:05.234
and then, on the 19th of June, in a small room in Edinburgh Castle, my baby was born.

00:38:05.294 --> 00:38:12.746
It took a long time, but at last you were in my arms.

00:38:12.806 --> 00:38:20.299
James, my son, I asked your father to come in.

00:38:20.359 --> 00:38:27.510
My Lord Henry, I said, This is our baby.

00:38:27.571 --> 00:38:30.142
Look at him, my lord.

00:38:30.202 --> 00:38:32.774
Take him in your arms.

00:38:32.834 --> 00:38:35.644
He is your son.

00:38:35.705 --> 00:38:39.076
Isn't he beautiful?

00:38:39.136 --> 00:38:44.370
But your father did not love me, James.

00:38:44.430 --> 00:38:51.308
Very often, after you were born, he slept with other women.

00:38:51.368 --> 00:38:57.156
I know that because he talked to everyone about it.

00:38:57.216 --> 00:39:02.128
I think he wanted people to know.

00:39:02.188 --> 00:39:10.484
And I am sorry, but I do not think he loved you, James.

00:39:10.544 --> 00:39:18.850
When I took you to church and gave you your name, he did not come.

00:39:18.910 --> 00:39:21.858
He wasn't interested.

00:39:21.918 --> 00:39:28.276
But because of him, David Ricchio was dead.

00:39:28.336 --> 00:39:31.972
I could never forget that.

00:39:32.033 --> 00:39:42.727
Never.

00:39:42.787 --> 00:39:53.909
Chapter 6.

00:39:53.970 --> 00:40:01.262
Kerker Field I had a new man to help me now.

00:40:01.322 --> 00:40:04.322
The Earl of Bothwell.

00:40:04.382 --> 00:40:07.744
A strong, clever man.

00:40:07.804 --> 00:40:10.214
He was older than me.

00:40:10.274 --> 00:40:13.775
He was not a boy like Darnley.

00:40:13.835 --> 00:40:18.156
He worked hard, and he could think.

00:40:18.216 --> 00:40:20.484
He was a good fighter.

00:40:20.544 --> 00:40:24.242
and he was not afraid of other men.

00:40:24.302 --> 00:40:30.574
Perhaps you are like him, James, my son.

00:40:30.634 --> 00:40:38.016
In January, your father, Darnley, was ill in Glasgow.

00:40:38.076 --> 00:40:43.728
I went to see him and took him back to Edinburgh.

00:40:43.788 --> 00:40:48.730
He was unhappy and afraid of people.

00:40:48.790 --> 00:40:52.790
He saw enemies behind every door.

00:40:52.850 --> 00:40:56.121
Poor stupid boy.

00:40:56.181 --> 00:40:59.632
He said he loved me again.

00:40:59.692 --> 00:41:05.513
I was angry, but I felt sorry for him too.

00:41:05.573 --> 00:41:08.684
He was very ill.

00:41:08.744 --> 00:41:13.284
It's not far now, Henry, I said.

00:41:13.344 --> 00:41:16.714
You can sleep in the castle.

00:41:16.774 --> 00:41:19.544
No, not there.

00:41:19.604 --> 00:41:22.626
Please, Mary," he said.

00:41:22.686 --> 00:41:25.828
I don't want to go into the castle.

00:41:25.888 --> 00:41:28.220
I'm afraid of it.

00:41:28.280 --> 00:41:31.191
But where do you want to go?

00:41:31.211 --> 00:41:33.763
I asked.

00:41:33.823 --> 00:41:41.038
Find me a little house outside the town and stay with me there.

00:41:41.098 --> 00:41:45.288
He said, we can be happy there.

00:41:45.348 --> 00:41:53.138
So I found him a small house called Kerkerfield outside Edinburgh.

00:41:53.198 --> 00:42:03.390
He stayed there in a room upstairs and sometimes I slept in a room downstairs.

00:42:03.451 --> 00:42:10.872
Darnley was often afraid and I visited him every day.

00:42:10.932 --> 00:42:15.567
Slowly he got better.

00:42:15.627 --> 00:42:23.093
On Sunday the 9th of February, there was a big wedding in Edinburgh.

00:42:23.153 --> 00:42:32.656
After the wedding, Bothwell and I walked out to Kirkafield to see Darnley and talk to him.

00:42:32.716 --> 00:42:39.028
Everyone sang and laughed and was very happy.

00:42:39.088 --> 00:42:43.825
At ten o'clock, I was tired.

00:42:43.885 --> 00:42:46.892
Good night, my lords."

00:42:46.952 --> 00:42:48.324
I said.

00:42:48.384 --> 00:42:51.406
I'm going downstairs to bed.

00:42:51.466 --> 00:42:55.759
Lord Botwell put his hand on my arm.

00:42:55.820 --> 00:43:02.305
Your majesty, he said, you can't sleep here now.

00:43:02.365 --> 00:43:04.496
Don't you remember?

00:43:04.556 --> 00:43:08.960
People are dancing and singing in town tonight.

00:43:09.020 --> 00:43:12.117
Everyone wants you to go.

00:43:12.177 --> 00:43:16.194
Oh, yes, I forgot.

00:43:16.254 --> 00:43:21.118
I said, of course people want to see me there.

00:43:21.178 --> 00:43:24.371
So, good night, Henry.

00:43:24.431 --> 00:43:26.513
Sleep well.

00:43:26.573 --> 00:43:30.526
Darnley was very unhappy.

00:43:30.586 --> 00:43:33.238
Please marry my love.

00:43:33.299 --> 00:43:36.100
Don't go, he said.

00:43:36.160 --> 00:43:39.547
Don't leave me here.

00:43:39.607 --> 00:43:43.712
But I did not love him now.

00:43:43.772 --> 00:43:47.484
I remembered the night when Riccio died.

00:43:47.544 --> 00:43:52.605
So I smiled and said, Goodnight Henry.

00:43:52.665 --> 00:43:55.126
Be a man now.

00:43:55.186 --> 00:43:59.678
Don't be afraid of the dark.

00:43:59.738 --> 00:44:04.629
Then I went downstairs with Lord Bothwell.

00:44:04.689 --> 00:44:09.549
Outside the house, we met one of Bothwell's men.

00:44:09.609 --> 00:44:16.722
He looked afraid, and there was something black on his face and hands.

00:44:16.742 --> 00:44:22.026
"'Jesus man, how dirty you are,' I said.

00:44:22.046 --> 00:44:25.740
"'Don't come near me with those hands.'"

00:44:25.800 --> 00:44:31.083
Normal lady, of course not, he said.

00:44:31.144 --> 00:44:37.034
He looked at both well for a minute, and then ran away quickly.

00:44:37.094 --> 00:44:43.054
I laughed, got on my horse, and forgot about it.

00:44:43.114 --> 00:44:50.839
I tell you before God, James, I did not kill your father.

00:44:50.899 --> 00:44:53.040
It was not me.

00:44:53.100 --> 00:44:57.884
I knew nothing about it, nothing.

00:44:57.944 --> 00:45:06.166
I sang and danced in town, and then went to bed in Edinburgh Castle.

00:45:06.226 --> 00:45:16.760
Then, at two o'clock in the morning, there was a sudden noise, a very big bang!

00:45:16.820 --> 00:45:20.824
Everybody heard it, all through the town.

00:45:20.884 --> 00:45:22.986
My God!

00:45:23.046 --> 00:45:26.298
I said, what's that?

00:45:26.358 --> 00:45:30.160
Everyone ran out of their rooms.

00:45:30.220 --> 00:45:33.613
Lord Bothwell was downstairs.

00:45:33.673 --> 00:45:37.014
Don't be afraid, ladies."

00:45:37.074 --> 00:45:40.944
He said, my men are outside.

00:45:41.004 --> 00:45:44.606
They're going to see what it is.

00:45:44.666 --> 00:45:49.867
After an hour, he came to see me.

00:45:49.927 --> 00:45:53.308
Please sit down, my lady.

00:45:53.368 --> 00:45:58.549
He said, I have some unhappy news.

00:45:58.609 --> 00:46:01.110
Yes, my lord.

00:46:01.170 --> 00:46:03.150
What is it?

00:46:03.210 --> 00:46:07.401
It's your husband, Lord Darnley.

00:46:07.461 --> 00:46:10.212
He is dead.

00:46:10.272 --> 00:46:13.552
But how?

00:46:13.612 --> 00:46:15.793
How did he die?

00:46:15.853 --> 00:46:18.504
Who killed him?

00:46:18.564 --> 00:46:21.335
I don't know, my lady.

00:46:21.395 --> 00:46:25.656
That bang, that was his house.

00:46:25.716 --> 00:46:30.776
Kerkerfield, it's not there anymore.

00:46:30.836 --> 00:46:32.816
What?

00:46:32.876 --> 00:46:36.147
And Darnley was inside?

00:46:36.207 --> 00:46:41.578
Well, no, my lady.

00:46:41.638 --> 00:46:44.748
Bothwell said slowly.

00:46:44.808 --> 00:46:51.730
My men found him in the garden, not in the house.

00:46:51.790 --> 00:46:59.672
He is wearing only night clothes, and there is no blood on him.

00:46:59.732 --> 00:47:02.360
But he is dead.

00:47:02.420 --> 00:47:04.678
I am sorry.

00:47:04.739 --> 00:47:06.840
Take me out there.

00:47:06.900 --> 00:47:08.802
I want to see him.

00:47:08.862 --> 00:47:10.372
Now.

00:47:10.432 --> 00:47:13.044
Yes, my lady.

00:47:13.104 --> 00:47:17.716
I went out to Kirkafield in the early morning.

00:47:17.776 --> 00:47:20.748
There was no house now.

00:47:20.808 --> 00:47:28.124
No walls, no doors, no windows, nothing.

00:47:28.185 --> 00:47:39.703
And there in the garden, a long way from the house was that poor, dead boy, my husband.

00:47:39.763 --> 00:47:46.026
I did not love him, but I cried then.

00:47:46.086 --> 00:47:52.930
He was your father, James, and I did not kill him.

00:47:52.990 --> 00:47:56.505
I don't know who killed him.

00:47:56.565 --> 00:48:02.132
but he had many enemies in Scotland.

00:48:02.192 --> 00:48:05.586
I was very afraid.

00:48:05.646 --> 00:48:11.492
I too had enemies and I often slept there.

00:48:11.552 --> 00:48:25.176
Perhaps someone wanted to kill me too.

00:48:25.236 --> 00:48:44.274
Chapter 7 Bothwell Soon everyone in Europe heard the news.

00:48:44.334 --> 00:48:50.848
The Queen of France and the Queen of England wrote angry letters to me.

00:48:50.908 --> 00:48:53.910
Who killed the king?

00:48:53.970 --> 00:48:55.991
They asked.

00:48:56.051 --> 00:49:00.344
I was very unhappy at this time, James.

00:49:00.404 --> 00:49:05.554
We looked for the killers, but we could not find them.

00:49:05.614 --> 00:49:08.803
Please believe me, James.

00:49:08.863 --> 00:49:12.844
The Scots lords are difficult men.

00:49:12.904 --> 00:49:21.298
Some were friends, some were enemies, but they changed all the time.

00:49:21.358 --> 00:49:28.781
Many people in Scotland said, Bothwell killed Lord Danley.

00:49:28.841 --> 00:49:37.373
I heard them outside the castle and in the town but I never believed it.

00:49:37.434 --> 00:49:47.560
People in Edinburgh sold horrible stories and pictures of Bothwell, the same day that Darnley died.

00:49:47.620 --> 00:49:50.572
It was too soon.

00:49:50.632 --> 00:50:00.149
Perhaps Darnley's killers wrote these stories about Bothwell before they killed Darnley.

00:50:00.209 --> 00:50:06.372
I don't think Lord Bothwell killed your father, James.

00:50:06.432 --> 00:50:11.434
He was a good friend to me in difficult times.

00:50:11.495 --> 00:50:18.868
He was a good, strong, clever man, and he worked hard.

00:50:18.928 --> 00:50:20.908
I liked that.

00:50:20.968 --> 00:50:25.199
A lot of women liked him, I think.

00:50:25.260 --> 00:50:31.174
Three times that spring, he asked me to marry him.

00:50:31.234 --> 00:50:37.249
He had a wife, and I could not marry again so soon.

00:50:37.309 --> 00:50:40.440
I asked him to wait.

00:50:40.500 --> 00:50:47.974
Then, on the 24th of April, I rode out of Edinburgh to the north.

00:50:48.034 --> 00:50:52.084
I had five or six friends with me.

00:50:52.144 --> 00:51:01.239
Six miles outside the town, Lord Boswell met us with an army.

00:51:01.299 --> 00:51:05.041
Why are you here, my lord?"

00:51:05.101 --> 00:51:06.762
I said.

00:51:06.822 --> 00:51:09.252
He smiled.

00:51:09.312 --> 00:51:14.605
Because I want to meet you, Mary, he said.

00:51:14.665 --> 00:51:19.267
I want you to come with me to my castle.

00:51:19.327 --> 00:51:26.220
He rode next to me, and his man rode between me and my friends.

00:51:26.280 --> 00:51:32.262
I was afraid and a little excited, too.

00:51:32.322 --> 00:51:38.236
But my Lord, you can't do this, I said.

00:51:38.296 --> 00:51:42.308
I don't want to come with you now.

00:51:42.368 --> 00:51:45.550
But I want you, Mary.

00:51:45.610 --> 00:51:49.781
He said, your friends can't stop me.

00:51:49.842 --> 00:51:53.873
I love you, and I want to marry you.

00:51:53.934 --> 00:51:57.486
What's wrong with that?

00:51:57.546 --> 00:52:00.757
I said nothing.

00:52:00.817 --> 00:52:03.428
What could I say?

00:52:03.488 --> 00:52:08.290
I liked him and he had an army.

00:52:08.350 --> 00:52:11.660
I had only six friends.

00:52:11.721 --> 00:52:21.592
So I rode with him to his castle in Dunbar and stayed there two weeks.

00:52:21.652 --> 00:52:28.914
And then he was a strong man and I was only a woman.

00:52:28.974 --> 00:52:31.984
And I did like him, James.

00:52:32.044 --> 00:52:35.105
I liked him very much.

00:52:35.165 --> 00:52:41.816
After two weeks in Dunbar, Bothwell and I rode back to Edinburgh.

00:52:41.876 --> 00:52:47.418
His wife did not want him, and was happy to divorce him.

00:52:47.478 --> 00:52:54.161
So, on the 15th of May 1567, I married him.

00:52:54.221 --> 00:52:59.384
He was a good man, James.

00:52:59.444 --> 00:53:02.686
A much better man than your father.

00:53:02.746 --> 00:53:08.168
I needed a strong man to help me rule the country.

00:53:08.228 --> 00:53:11.670
But I was wrong.

00:53:11.730 --> 00:53:15.002
I understand that now.

00:53:15.062 --> 00:53:22.722
All the Scots lords were afraid of Bothwell, and many of them were his enemies.

00:53:22.782 --> 00:53:32.866
They had an army, and on the 15th of June, Bothwell and I rode out to fight them.

00:53:32.926 --> 00:53:37.209
We met them at Carbury Hill.

00:53:37.269 --> 00:53:47.069
It was a hot day, and the two big armies stood and looked and waited.

00:53:47.130 --> 00:53:56.726
Their army had a big flag with a picture of your poor, dead father, darnly on it.

00:53:56.786 --> 00:54:05.270
Under the picture, there were the words, find my killers, oh God.

00:54:05.330 --> 00:54:08.512
Come on, my lord.

00:54:08.572 --> 00:54:14.084
I said to Bothwell, our army is better than theirs.

00:54:14.145 --> 00:54:17.202
Let's fight them.

00:54:17.262 --> 00:54:23.140
Bothwell rode up and down, and talked to his men.

00:54:23.200 --> 00:54:26.461
But they didn't want to fight.

00:54:26.521 --> 00:54:32.584
They talked, and looked at the flag, and waited.

00:54:32.644 --> 00:54:37.125
Then, some of them walked home.

00:54:37.185 --> 00:54:45.498
At five o'clock that evening, Lord Keir Kaldi rode from his army to talk to us.

00:54:45.558 --> 00:54:52.723
He said to me, My lady, leave your husband and come with us.

00:54:52.783 --> 00:54:56.696
We don't want men to die.

00:54:56.756 --> 00:55:05.124
And so, because our men didn't want to fight, I went with him.

00:55:05.184 --> 00:55:09.126
It was a very bad day for me.

00:55:09.187 --> 00:55:11.757
They took me back to Edinburgh.

00:55:11.817 --> 00:55:15.078
And people in the streets screamed at me.

00:55:15.138 --> 00:55:16.519
Kill the woman.

00:55:16.579 --> 00:55:19.240
She sleeps with her husband's killer.

00:55:19.300 --> 00:55:21.862
We want James to be king.

00:55:21.922 --> 00:55:24.652
Kill her now.

00:55:24.712 --> 00:55:29.014
I was unhappy and afraid.

00:55:29.074 --> 00:55:32.596
And I was pregnant again.

00:55:32.656 --> 00:55:36.870
They took me to Lochleven Castle.

00:55:36.930 --> 00:55:40.914
and put me in a room like a prison.

00:55:40.974 --> 00:55:45.308
There I did not eat for two weeks.

00:55:45.368 --> 00:55:52.954
And Bothwell's children, there were two babies, were born dead.

00:55:53.014 --> 00:55:56.086
I nearly died too.

00:55:56.146 --> 00:56:02.070
I was so angry and tired and ill.

00:56:02.130 --> 00:56:10.014
Then one day after the babies died, Lord Lindsey gave me a letter.

00:56:10.074 --> 00:56:20.850
It said, I, Mary, Queen of Scots, give the kingdom of Scotland to my son, James.

00:56:20.910 --> 00:56:28.062
From today, James is the new king of Scots.

00:56:28.122 --> 00:56:41.029
But, because he is a child, the Earl of Moray, my half-brother, can rule the country for him.

00:56:41.089 --> 00:56:50.212
Because I was afraid and tired and ill, I wrote my name on the letter.

00:56:50.272 --> 00:56:52.270
Mary.

00:56:52.330 --> 00:56:56.152
But it is not important, James.

00:56:56.212 --> 00:56:59.144
It doesn't change anything.

00:56:59.205 --> 00:57:01.746
I am Queen of Scots.

00:57:01.806 --> 00:57:03.446
Not you.

00:57:03.506 --> 00:57:07.189
That letter changes nothing.

00:57:07.249 --> 00:57:15.084
Bothwell went over the sea and died in a prison in Denmark.

00:57:15.144 --> 00:57:25.624
I was a prisoner in Lachleven for a year A lot of people in Europe were angry about that.

00:57:25.684 --> 00:57:29.536
Queen Elizabeth wrote to the Earl of Moray.

00:57:29.596 --> 00:57:34.500
You cannot keep a queen in prison, she said.

00:57:34.560 --> 00:57:37.582
It is very wrong.

00:57:37.642 --> 00:57:40.684
I was pleased about that.

00:57:40.745 --> 00:57:43.807
But Moray didn't listen.

00:57:43.867 --> 00:57:51.517
Lord Douglas lived in the castle, and his young son William liked me.

00:57:51.577 --> 00:57:56.783
One day there was a wedding in the castle.

00:57:56.843 --> 00:58:01.544
People sang and danced and drank.

00:58:01.604 --> 00:58:07.106
William Douglas gave me some old women's clothes.

00:58:07.166 --> 00:58:14.227
I put the clothes on and walked quietly out of the castle with him.

00:58:14.287 --> 00:58:20.929
He shut the castle door behind us to keep his father's friends in.

00:58:20.990 --> 00:58:28.485
Then we got on some horses, and rode away through the night.

00:58:28.545 --> 00:58:32.418
All my friends came back to me.

00:58:32.478 --> 00:58:35.570
Soon I had a big army.

00:58:35.630 --> 00:58:39.563
Mary is our queen again, people said.

00:58:39.624 --> 00:58:42.466
Give her back her son.

00:58:42.526 --> 00:58:49.364
You were in Earl Moray's castle, James, so I came to fight him.

00:58:49.424 --> 00:58:57.120
I rode with my army to Langside near Glasgow and there.

00:58:57.180 --> 00:59:00.142
There, James.

00:59:00.203 --> 00:59:03.684
There, my son.

00:59:03.745 --> 00:59:06.936
I lost the fight.

00:59:06.996 --> 00:59:10.458
I am so sorry.

00:59:10.518 --> 00:59:16.372
I had many good, strong men in my army.

00:59:16.432 --> 00:59:20.505
But oh, Moray's men were stronger.

00:59:20.566 --> 00:59:26.752
Many of my men died, and some ran away.

00:59:26.812 --> 00:59:31.516
After the fight I ran away too.

00:59:31.576 --> 00:59:40.373
I did not want to go to prison again, so I rode south to England.

00:59:40.434 --> 00:59:45.078
Queen Elizabeth wants to help me, I thought.

00:59:45.138 --> 00:59:47.360
She understands.

00:59:47.420 --> 00:59:53.046
She wrote to Moray, and she is a queen, like me.

00:59:53.107 --> 01:00:02.944
I can come back to Scotland with her army, kill Moray, and find my baby son James.

01:00:03.004 --> 01:00:07.438
I am in England, but I am free.

01:00:07.498 --> 01:00:09.160
I can try again.

01:00:09.180 --> 01:00:13.824
I was wrong about that too.

01:00:13.884 --> 01:00:24.827
Very wrong.

01:00:24.887 --> 01:00:42.884
Chapter 8 England Elizabeth didn't give me her army.

01:00:42.944 --> 01:00:46.027
She put me in prison.

01:00:46.087 --> 01:00:48.839
You know this, James.

01:00:48.899 --> 01:00:53.992
It is the story of your life, not mine.

01:00:54.053 --> 01:01:02.317
I was 25 years old when I came to England, and I am 45 now.

01:01:02.377 --> 01:01:07.648
20 years in English prisons.

01:01:07.708 --> 01:01:12.338
Moray told lies about me.

01:01:12.398 --> 01:01:17.730
Mary and Bothwell killed Darnley, he said.

01:01:17.790 --> 01:01:25.171
Mary slept with Richeo and Bothwell and killed her husband.

01:01:25.231 --> 01:01:27.701
But it's not true.

01:01:27.761 --> 01:01:30.592
They're all lies, James.

01:01:30.652 --> 01:01:32.947
Wicked lies.

01:01:33.008 --> 01:01:41.290
They only said these things because I am a woman and a Catholic.

01:01:41.350 --> 01:01:46.594
And they don't want a Catholic queen in Scotland.

01:01:46.654 --> 01:01:50.138
They want a Protestant king.

01:01:50.158 --> 01:01:54.942
A king like you, James.

01:01:55.002 --> 01:02:00.514
Why, James, my son, don't you help me?

01:02:00.574 --> 01:02:05.846
Why are you friendly with Elizabeth, my enemy?

01:02:05.906 --> 01:02:10.250
You don't want me back in Scotland, do you?

01:02:10.310 --> 01:02:14.744
You believe these lies, don't you?

01:02:14.804 --> 01:02:20.098
You talk to Moray and his friends every day.

01:02:20.158 --> 01:02:23.962
But they lied about me, James.

01:02:24.022 --> 01:02:28.582
Moray and his friends killed Riccio.

01:02:28.642 --> 01:02:32.022
They killed your father too.

01:02:32.082 --> 01:02:35.334
They stole my husband, both well.

01:02:35.394 --> 01:02:37.025
Stole my son.

01:02:37.045 --> 01:02:42.259
Stole my son's love.

01:02:42.319 --> 01:02:45.402
I'm sorry, James.

01:02:45.462 --> 01:02:47.444
Forgive me.

01:02:47.504 --> 01:02:51.616
Sometimes I get very angry.

01:02:51.676 --> 01:03:02.058
It is difficult not to be angry when you are in prison for 20 years.

01:03:02.118 --> 01:03:06.680
Elizabeth didn't know what to do.

01:03:06.740 --> 01:03:09.702
Sometimes she believed Murray.

01:03:09.762 --> 01:03:12.326
Sometimes she didn't.

01:03:12.386 --> 01:03:18.864
She was afraid to kill me, because I was a queen.

01:03:18.924 --> 01:03:27.587
She was afraid to let me go free, because I have friends in England.

01:03:27.648 --> 01:03:44.914
The English Catholics want me to be Queen of England, not her and she is a woman with no husband and no son, so she hates me too.

01:03:44.974 --> 01:03:55.652
Sometimes the English Catholics write to me and ask me for help, and sometimes I write to them.

01:03:55.712 --> 01:04:02.012
Sometimes Elizabeth's men find these letters.

01:04:02.072 --> 01:04:08.362
The English Protestants want to kill me because of these letters.

01:04:08.422 --> 01:04:13.144
You are a wicked woman, they say.

01:04:13.204 --> 01:04:20.607
You killed your husband, Darnley, and now you want to kill our Queen Elizabeth.

01:04:20.667 --> 01:04:23.394
You're going to die.

01:04:23.454 --> 01:04:28.702
I did not kill my husband, I said.

01:04:28.762 --> 01:04:35.114
And when I came to England, I did not want to kill your queen.

01:04:35.174 --> 01:04:38.125
I asked her for help.

01:04:38.185 --> 01:04:42.266
I wanted to go back to Scotland.

01:04:42.326 --> 01:04:48.632
But my lords, she put me in prison for 20 years.

01:04:48.692 --> 01:04:54.986
Twenty years, my lords, I want to be free.

01:04:55.046 --> 01:04:58.327
Don't you understand that?

01:04:58.387 --> 01:05:07.559
When men write to me and try to help me, then yes, sometimes I write back.

01:05:07.619 --> 01:05:09.539
Why not?

01:05:09.599 --> 01:05:11.640
Is that wicked?

01:05:11.700 --> 01:05:14.800
Do you think?

01:05:14.860 --> 01:05:18.436
They didn't listen.

01:05:18.496 --> 01:05:23.151
Of course not, they want to kill me.

01:05:23.211 --> 01:05:27.472
And so they wrote to Queen Elizabeth.

01:05:27.532 --> 01:05:37.724
And now I sit here, in fathering a castle, and wait for her to answer.

01:05:37.784 --> 01:05:43.102
I do not want to die, James my son.

01:05:43.163 --> 01:05:50.028
But I do not want to live all my life in an English prison.

01:05:50.088 --> 01:05:55.034
I am old and tired of life.

01:05:55.094 --> 01:06:10.311
Think well of me, James, my son.

01:06:10.371 --> 01:06:29.570
Chapter 9 A Death Queen Mary stopped writing then.

01:06:29.630 --> 01:06:40.860
Yesterday afternoon, the 7th of February 1587, we heard a horse outside our window.

01:06:40.920 --> 01:06:43.873
Mary looked out.

01:06:43.933 --> 01:06:49.082
There was a man there, on the road from London.

01:06:49.142 --> 01:06:54.452
He had a letter from the Queen of England.

01:06:54.512 --> 01:07:02.408
In the evening, an Englishman, Lord Shrewsbury came to see Mary.

01:07:02.468 --> 01:07:09.784
I'm sorry, my lady, he said, but I have a letter from my queen.

01:07:09.844 --> 01:07:14.938
You're going to die tomorrow.

01:07:14.998 --> 01:07:18.526
Mary did not move.

01:07:18.586 --> 01:07:23.224
when she asked quietly.

01:07:23.284 --> 01:07:33.062
At half past eight in the morning, he said, I am very sorry, my lady.

01:07:33.122 --> 01:07:36.104
He went away.

01:07:36.164 --> 01:07:40.297
We did not sleep much that night.

01:07:40.358 --> 01:07:49.270
We talked and prayed to God, and she gave me her letter to her son, James.

01:07:49.330 --> 01:07:53.970
Give it to him, Bess, please."

01:07:54.030 --> 01:07:56.072
She said.

01:07:56.132 --> 01:07:59.704
And tell him how I died.

01:07:59.764 --> 01:08:03.908
Yes, my lady, I said.

01:08:03.968 --> 01:08:09.492
And so now I am going to tell you King James.

01:08:09.553 --> 01:08:13.340
This is how your mother died.

01:08:13.400 --> 01:08:20.856
At six o'clock, she got up, prayed and dressed.

01:08:20.917 --> 01:08:31.590
She put on a red petticoat first, then a black dress and a white veil over the dress.

01:08:31.649 --> 01:08:36.971
The veil came from her head to her feet.

01:08:37.030 --> 01:08:42.780
She could see out through it, but we could not see her face.

01:08:42.841 --> 01:08:47.752
She looked like a woman on her wedding day.

01:08:47.812 --> 01:08:54.156
When the Englishmen came, we went downstairs with her.

01:08:54.217 --> 01:09:02.552
Her little dog walked beside her under the veil, but the Englishmen didn't see that.

01:09:02.612 --> 01:09:07.315
Six of us went into a big room with her.

01:09:07.376 --> 01:09:11.662
A hundred people stood and watched.

01:09:11.721 --> 01:09:15.887
A Protestant churchman came to talk to her.

01:09:15.946 --> 01:09:22.538
My lady, he said, pray with me.

01:09:22.598 --> 01:09:36.004
No, she said, thank you, but no, I was born a Catholic and I'm going to die a Catholic.

01:09:36.064 --> 01:09:40.486
I think God understands that.

01:09:40.546 --> 01:09:46.730
She prayed for five minutes and then stood up.

01:09:46.790 --> 01:09:50.944
The executioner came towards her.

01:09:51.004 --> 01:09:59.702
He was a big, strong man with an axe and something black over his face.

01:09:59.762 --> 01:10:04.626
I'm sorry, my lady, he said.

01:10:04.686 --> 01:10:08.329
I don't hate you, but this is my work.

01:10:08.388 --> 01:10:11.091
Please forgive me.

01:10:11.151 --> 01:10:14.443
Of course, I forgive you.

01:10:14.503 --> 01:10:24.668
Mary said, I am old and tired, and you're going to open my prison doors for me.

01:10:24.728 --> 01:10:28.198
I am going to see God.

01:10:28.258 --> 01:10:31.660
Do your work well.

01:10:31.720 --> 01:10:36.722
Then she looked at me and her friends.

01:10:36.782 --> 01:10:42.361
Don't cry for me, ladies, she said.

01:10:42.421 --> 01:10:46.700
Please don't cry now.

01:10:46.760 --> 01:10:54.066
She could not walk to the block so the executioner helped her.

01:10:54.126 --> 01:11:03.374
He took off her white veil and then he took off her black dress and put it on the floor.

01:11:03.434 --> 01:11:10.342
She stood there in her red petticoat with a smile on her face.

01:11:10.402 --> 01:11:15.996
Then the executioner put something over her eyes.

01:11:16.056 --> 01:11:22.280
Very slowly Mary put her head on the block.

01:11:22.340 --> 01:11:30.544
The Lord, my God, is my one true friend, she said.

01:11:30.604 --> 01:11:37.472
I give my life, O God, into your hands.

01:11:37.532 --> 01:11:58.196
then the executioner lifted his axe once, twice, oh God, three times, and her head, her poor, poor head, fell on the floor.

01:11:58.256 --> 01:12:03.108
It was very quiet in the room after that.

01:12:03.168 --> 01:12:07.359
It is a little thing ahead.

01:12:07.419 --> 01:12:09.930
A very little thing.

01:12:09.990 --> 01:12:13.432
But there was so much blood.

01:12:13.492 --> 01:12:16.884
Blood on her red petticoat.

01:12:16.944 --> 01:12:21.688
Blood on her black dress and her white veil.

01:12:21.748 --> 01:12:25.019
Blood on the executioner's shoes.

01:12:25.079 --> 01:12:27.861
Blood all over the floor.

01:12:27.920 --> 01:12:29.522
Blood.

01:12:29.582 --> 01:12:33.170
Blood everywhere.

01:12:33.230 --> 01:12:38.491
We all looked and said nothing.

01:12:38.551 --> 01:12:44.436
The executioner put down his axe and stood quietly.

01:12:44.496 --> 01:12:58.869
And then Mary's little dog came out from under her bloody dress and veil and walked slowly, unhappily through the blood towards her head.

01:12:58.929 --> 01:13:05.574
My Lord, the story of your poor mother's life finishes here.

01:13:05.634 --> 01:13:10.046
We, her friends, cry for her.

01:13:10.106 --> 01:13:13.636
But that is how your mother died.

01:13:13.696 --> 01:13:17.298
She died like a queen.

01:13:17.358 --> 01:13:22.049
A good lady and a famous queen.

01:13:22.109 --> 01:13:25.200
Mary, Queen of Scots.

